# Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored.
#
# ONE entry, a genuine false positive:
# - tor_status.py write_to_temp_then_move() prints content via redact_credentials(),
#   which masks every credential option (Socks5ProxyPassword, *ProxyAuthenticator,
#   HashedControlPassword, ...) to [REDACTED] before the print; CodeQL does not
#   recognize the sanitizer, so it reports a clear-text-logging finding here.
#
# NOT baselined (deliberately left reported, not suppressed):
# - py/clear-text-storage-sensitive-data at tor_status.py comm_file.write(): the Tor
#   config IPC file holds the plaintext proxy credential, but it is world-readable
#   (tmpfiles 0666 in a 0777 dir) -- a real exposure, flagged for the permission fix,
#   so it must keep surfacing until that is addressed.
# The torrc_gen.py DEBUG prints that CodeQL also flagged were removed (they leaked
# the custom bridge descriptor), so those findings no longer exist.
